lesson: 255
title: Getting everyone there
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A return ticket takes you there and brings you back: it is 2 journeys.
explain: When the price is given for one journey, a return ticket costs 2 times that price.
explain: 3 people buy return tickets at $4 a journey: each ticket is 2 × $4 = $8, and 3 × $8 = $24.
vars: a=name b=name f=2..6 p=2..9
answer: f * 2 * p
exercise: {a}'s family of {f} buys return tickets on the bus. One journey costs ${p}. How many dollars do they pay?
exercise: {f} friends take the train to the beach and back on return tickets. A single journey costs ${p}. How much do they pay in all?
exercise: The ferry charges ${p} for each journey. {a} buys return tickets for {f} people. What is the total cost in dollars?
exercise: A journey on the tram costs ${p}. How many dollars do {f} children spend on return tickets?
exercise: {a} and {b} go to the zoo by bus with their family, {f} people in all, themselves included. Each journey is ${p}, and everyone has a return ticket. How many dollars are paid?
exercise: return tix for the {f} of us, ${p} a journey. how much
exercise: bus is ${p} each way, we're {f+1}, no {f} going. returns for everyone, total?
exercise: {f} of us going to the city on the train, ${p} a journey, oh and {a} forgot their card again. how much for returns
exercise: mum says get returns for all {f} of us, it's ${p} one way. how much is that
exercise: ferry's ${p} a trip innit, {f} of us need returns. how much altogether
test: What do return tickets cost for {f} travellers if a one-way journey is ${p}?
test: {a} pays for a family outing: {f} return tickets, with every journey priced at ${p}. How many dollars does {a.he} hand over?
test: Each journey on the coach costs ${p}. Find the total cost of return tickets for a group of {f}.
test: {f} returns, ${p} a journey. how much
test: {a} reckons {f} returns at ${p} a journey is ${f*p}. nope. what's it really
test: {f} of us on the tram there n back, ${p} each way, {b} brought snacks. total cost in dollars
exam: It is given that {f.words} persons each purchase a return ticket, the fare for a single journey being {p} dollars. Determine the aggregate expenditure incurred.
exam: A party of {f} travellers procures return tickets on a service charging ${p} per journey. Ascertain the total amount payable, in dollars.
exam: Compute the total cost, expressed in dollars, of return tickets in respect of {f} passengers, whereas the tariff for one journey is ${p}.
exam: Pursuant to a fare of {p} dollars per journey, state the sum disbursed by a family of {f} for return tickets for every member thereof.
exercise: {a}'s family was {f+1}, but they are {f} since Grandma passed away. They all buy return bus tickets to visit her grave, and one journey costs ${p}. How many dollars do they pay?
exercise: dad got the boot so no car any more, bloody bus it is. {f} of us, return tickets, ${p} a trip. how many dollars, what a rip-off?
test: {a}'s uncle said the trip would be very reasonably priced: {f} travellers, each paying ${p} for the journey out and ${p} for the journey home. What is the total in dollars?
